# XCU break
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The special built-in utilities are described inside
# utilities/V3_chap02.html (the page utilities/break.html only redirects
# there), so anchors name V3_chap02.html and the .cov file accounts for
# the units by hand.

assertion  XCU.break.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/shall exit from the
class      required
says       Without an operand, break leaves the innermost for, while or
           until loop and execution continues after that loop.
test       t/001-innermost.sh

assertion  XCU.break.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/shall exit from the
class      required
says       break n leaves the nth enclosing loop; break 1 is the same as
           break.
test       t/002-nth-loop.sh

assertion  XCU.break.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/outermost
class      required
says       When n is greater than the number of enclosing loops, break
           leaves the outermost enclosing loop.
test       t/003-too-large.sh

assertion  XCU.break.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/Contained in a compound-list associated with the loop
class      required
says       A break written in the condition list of a while or until loop
           leaves that loop.
test       t/004-in-condition.sh

assertion  XCU.break.005
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/lexically encloses
class      required
says       break inside if, case and brace-group commands that are
           themselves inside a loop still leaves the loop.
test       t/005-nested-compound.sh

assertion  XCU.break.006
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/not an unsigned decimal integer
class      required
says       A break whose operand is not a positive decimal integer returns a
           non-zero status (or the shell exits with a non-zero status); it
           never acts as a normal break or as a no-op returning zero.
test       t/006-bad-operand.sh

assertion  XCU.break.007
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#STDOUT/Not used
class      required
says       break writes nothing to standard output.
test       t/007-no-stdout.sh
